{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786504428,"nonce":"skdlLKClDbpO/fJ+uj+f514Nx74=","title":"Nothing writes an actor or a comment into the notification view: every `by(who)` in the Slack renderer is empty and every `comment` reply is a bare emoji","was":"**What is wrong.** The notification view has two ways to learn who caused a fact and what they said, and **neither is ever written in production**. `ViewRequest.Actor` (`internal/notification/service/view.go:73`) and `ViewRequest.Comment` (`:75`) are read by `project` at `:133` and `:107`; both production callers of `Build` construct a `ViewRequest` with only `Notification` set. The fallback at `:135` reads `domain.Snapshot.Actor` (`internal/notification/domain/snapshot.go:285`), which the snapshot repository never scans into, and `Snapshot.Comment` (`:286`) is in the same state. So `NotificationView.Actor` is always `nil` and `NotificationView.Comment` is always `\"\"`, in every deployment, on every card."}]}